#### 8. Exception Handling — `addNullSkuManualCatch` (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

Manual `try/catch/fail` is error-prone (catching broad `Exception` can mask wrong exception types) and verbose. JUnit 5 has `assertThrows`.

**Refactor:**

```java
@Test
void addNullSkuThrows() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

